<p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 14 February 2026</p>

<p>This Privacy Policy explains how Skribl ("We", "Us", or "Our") handles information when You use the Skribl application (the "Service").</p>

<h2>1. Overview</h2>
<p>Skribl is designed to operate without requiring personal information such as your name or email address.</p>
<p>The Service does not require user registration and does not request personal contact details.</p>

<h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

<h3>Device-Associated Account Identifier</h3>
<p>When You first use the Application, a technical account identifier is created and stored in a secure cookie on Your Device. This identifier allows the Service to associate Your notes with Your Device.</p>
<p>This identifier:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Does not contain Your name or email address;</li>
  <li>Does not directly identify You as an individual;</li>
  <li>Is used solely to retrieve and store Your notes.</li>
</ul>

<h3>User-Created Content</h3>
<p>The Service allows You to create handwritten or drawn notes, which are stored as image files on our servers and associated with Your device account.</p>
<p>Your notes:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Are private to Your device-associated account;</li>
  <li>Are not visible to other users;</li>
  <li>Are not shared with third parties.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Technical Data</h3>
<p>Basic technical information (such as IP address and standard web request logs) may be processed by our hosting provider for security, debugging, and operational purposes.</p>
<p>We do not use analytics services, tracking technologies, or advertising identifiers.</p>

<h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
<p>We use information solely to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Provide and maintain the Service;</li>
  <li>Store and retrieve Your notes;</li>
  <li>Maintain the security and integrity of the Service.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Data Sharing</h2>
<p>We do not sell, rent, or share Your data with advertisers or third parties for marketing purposes.</p>
<p>Your data is processed only as necessary to provide the Service, including through our hosting provider.</p>

<h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
<p>Your notes remain stored on our servers and associated with Your device account unless:</p>
<ul>
  <li>You manually delete them; or</li>
  <li>The device-associated session is permanently lost.</li>
</ul>
<p>If You uninstall the Application, clear Your device cookies, or lose access to the device, Your notes may not be recoverable.</p>

<h2>6. Data Deletion</h2>
<p>You may delete individual notes within the Application.</p>
<p>If You wish to request deletion of all data associated with Your device account, You may contact us using the details below.</p>

<h2>7. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>The Service is not directed to children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.</p>
<p>If You believe that a child has provided personal information to Us, please contact Us and We will take appropriate steps to remove such information.</p>

<h2>8. Security</h2>
<p>We take reasonable measures to protect stored data. However, no system is completely secure, and We cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

<h2>9. Links to Other Websites</h2>
<p>The Service may contain links to third-party websites. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of those websites.</p>

<h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page and the "Last updated" date will be revised accordingly.</p>
<p>Continued use of the Service after changes become effective constitutes acceptance of the updated Privacy Policy.</p>

<h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
<p>If You have any questions about this Privacy Policy, You may contact us at:</p>
<p><a href="mailto:hello@matthewblott.com">hello@matthewblott.com</a></p>

